<%# One photo of a post: its thumbnail, its two controls, its id, and its alt text.

    ⚠️ **The fields render in THIS order in every tile.** The names are `posts[][photos][]` and
    `posts[][alts][]`, and Rack reads the two arrays by position. A tile that omits one field
    would move each alt text after it by one. The order of the tiles in the document IS the order
    of the photos, thus a reorder moves the tile and rewrites nothing.

    A tile is a ROW, as a post of the thread is: the grip, the thumbnail, the alt text, and the
    remove control. The tiles stack in a column, thus the alt text field takes the width.

    ⚠️ The GRIP carries `draggable`, and never the tile: a draggable tile takes the pointer away
    from the alt field inside it. The grip is a button and it takes the arrow keys, because a drag
    needs a pointer and this page must work without one. %>
<%# ⚠️ `data-photo-alt-url` is the path of the Generate control of THIS tile. The server writes it
    here, and the answer of the upload writes it for a new tile, thus the JavaScript builds no
    path. The control renders only when Claude has a key, and it is disabled while the tile has
    no id. %>
<div class="social-photo" data-social-post-target="photo"
     data-photo-alt-url="<%= social_photo_alt_path(photo.id) if photo.id.present? %>">
  <%# The id that the upload answered with. It is empty while the upload is out, and the action
      drops such a pair with its alt text. It is first because it renders nothing. %>
  <input type="hidden" name="posts[][photos][]" value="<%= photo.id %>" data-photo-id>

  <wa-button class="social-photo__grip" appearance="plain" size="small" draggable="true"
             data-action="dragstart->social-post#dragStartPhoto dragend->social-post#dragEndPhoto
                          keydown->social-post#movePhotoByKey">
    <%= raw icon_svg("classic", "light", "grip-dots-vertical") %>
    <span class="wa-visually-hidden"><%= t(".reorder_photo") %></span>
  </wa-button>

  <div class="social-photo__media">
    <%# ⚠️ No handler on `error`. A thumbnail that fails to load must not take the photo off the
        draft: the submit refuses a photo that is gone, with a message. %>
    <img class="social-photo__image" alt=""
         <% if photo.id.present? %>src="<%= social_photo_path(photo.id) %>"<% end %>
         data-photo-image>
    <%# It spins while the upload is out. It needs a rule for `[hidden]`; refer to _social.scss. %>
    <wa-spinner class="social-photo__spinner" data-photo-spinner hidden></wa-spinner>
  </div>

  <div class="social-photo__text">
    <%# ⚠️ No `maxlength`: it measures UTF-16 code units, and Bluesky counts graphemes. The line
        below says when the text is past the limit, and the submit button then stays off. %>
    <wa-textarea class="social-photo__alt" name="posts[][alts][]" label="<%= t(".photo_alt") %>"
                 rows="3" resize="auto" size="small" value="<%= photo.alt %>"
                 data-photo-alt data-action="input->social-post#countAlt">
    </wa-textarea>
    <span class="social-photo__alt-over wa-caption-s" data-photo-alt-over hidden></span>

    <%# ⚠️ `type="button"`, as each button of a dialog carries: a <wa-button> is form-associated,
        and one with no type in a form could submit the draft. The controller sets `loading` and
        `disabled` together while the request is out, thus a second click starts nothing. %>
    <% if alt_text %>
      <wa-button class="social-photo__generate" type="button" appearance="outlined" size="small"
                 data-photo-generate data-action="click->social-post#generateAlt"
                 <%= "disabled" if photo.id.blank? %>>
        <%= slotted_icon_svg("classic", "light", "sparkles") %>
        <%= t(".generate_alt") %>
      </wa-button>
    <% end %>
  </div>

  <wa-button class="social-photo__remove" appearance="plain" size="small"
             data-action="click->social-post#removePhoto">
    <%= raw icon_svg("classic", "light", "circle-xmark") %>
    <span class="wa-visually-hidden"><%= t(".remove_photo") %></span>
  </wa-button>
</div>
